            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-112323-libgssapi-krb5-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-112323 high vulnerability for libgssapi-krb5-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The AUTH_GSSAPI handler in lib/rpc/svc_auth_gssapi.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) 1.5.2 and later allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (memory exhaustion in kadmind) by sending repeated failed AUTH_GSSAPI_INIT requests. Each failed request allocates client state that is only freed after a 15-minute expiration timeout, allowing an attacker to accumulate memory faster than it is reclaimed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112323",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-112323\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libgssapi-krb5-2\nVersion: 1.21.3-5+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-112323](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112323)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-112323**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libgssapi-krb5-2  | 1.21.3-5+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-112323](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112323)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgssapi-krb5-2@1.21.3-5%2Bdeb13u1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=krb5"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-119079-libgssapi-krb5-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119079 high vulnerability for libgssapi-krb5-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "decode_sequence_of() in lib/krb5/asn.1/asn1_encode.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) 1.11 and later grows the decoded element array one entry at a time, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption in the KDC) by sending an unauthenticated AS-REQ or TGS-REQ with a large number of elements in a SEQUENCE OF field over TCP."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-119079",
