            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-87863-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-87863 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An authenticated HTTPS origin can supply an HSTS `max-age` value that the parser accepts, but time serialization later fails to process. On 64-bit systems, extreme max-age values compute an absolute expiry within standard time integer limits that exceeds calendar time structure bounds. During cache saves, the original HSTS file is truncated before writing a temporary replacement; when serialization fails, the temporary file is deleted, leaving an empty or partial cache. Because the save error is silently ignored during cleanup, curl exits successfully despite the data loss."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-87863\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.14.1-2+deb13u7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-87863](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-87863**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | curl  | 8.14.1-2+deb13u7  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-87863](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-87863)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.14.1-2%2Bdeb13u7?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92386-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92386 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When writing a long cookie name and value to a Netscape cookie jar, a remote HTTP server can make `curl` write a record that exceeds its line-length parsing limit. Consequently, any subsequent `curl` invocation reading from that same cookie jar using `--cookie` silently aborts parsing prematurely upon encountering the too long line, ignoring all subsequent valid cookies in the file."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92386",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92386\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.14.1-2+deb13u7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-92386](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92386)",
