              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When `CURLOPT_INTERFACE` (or the command line tool's `--interface` option) is set with one of the documented prefixes (`if!`, `host!`, `ifhost!`), that binding is not part of the connection reuse key, so a later transfer asking for a different source can silently reuse an existing connection and go out from the earlier transfer's source address"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107929",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107929\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libcurl4t64\nVersion: 8.14.1-2+deb13u7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-107929](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107929)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107929**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libcurl4t64  | 8.14.1-2+deb13u7  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-107929](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107929)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4t64@8.14.1-2%2Bdeb13u7?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82560-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-82560 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhaustion formatting a POD document whose =over nesting drives the margin to the output width.  Each =over adds its indent to the margin, which wrap() subtracts from the output width to get the space available for text. When that space reaches zero, the line-splitting substitution matches the empty string, and the loop consumes no input while appending the margin padding on every pass.  Formatting an attacker-supplied POD document never returns, and the output grows until memory is exhausted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-82560](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.40.1-6+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-82560](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-82560)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.40.1-6%2Bdeb13u1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
