            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107161-libsasl2-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107161 high vulnerability for libsasl2-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A heap-based buffer overflow flaw was found in Cyrus SASL. The add_to_challenge() function in the DIGEST-MD5 plugin computes the size of the buffer needed for a challenge/response field before DIGEST-MD5 quoting is applied, but does not recompute that size when quoting (escaping special characters) makes the value longer. The under-sized buffer is then passed to strcat(), causing a heap-based out-of-bounds write whose size depends on attacker-controlled input. A malicious or on-path DIGEST-MD5 (or HTTP Digest) server can trigger this flaw in a connecting client by supplying a crafted challenge field, such as realm or nonce, most likely resulting in a crash of the client application."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107161",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-107161\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libsasl2-2\nVersion: 2.1.28+dfsg1-9\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-107161](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107161)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-107161**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libsasl2-2  | 2.1.28+dfsg1-9  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-107161](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-107161)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libsasl2-2@2.1.28%2Bdfsg1-9?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=cyrus-sasl2"
