            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9545-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9545 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In this scenario, libcurl first uses a proper HTTP/3 server for the initial transfers, and when it makes a second transfer to the same site it has been replaced by the attacker's impostor machine - without a valid certificate.  When libcurl returns to the hostname the second time with a cached SSL session (`CURLOPT_SSL_SESSIONID_CACHE` is not disabled) and early data enabled (the `CURLSSLOPT_EARLYDATA` bit is set in `CURLOPT_SSL_OPTIONS`), libcurl might send off the second request's bytes on that new connection *before* enforcing the certificate verification failure. Potentially leaking sensitive information."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9545",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9545\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.14.1-2+deb13u7\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-9545](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9545)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9545**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | curl  | 8.14.1-2+deb13u7  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-9545](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9545)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.14.1-2%2Bdeb13u7?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
