            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-119379-libsqlite3-0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119379 high vulnerability for libsqlite3-0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite before 3.54.0 built with the session extension contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in sqlite3changeset_apply() that allows attackers to corrupt heap memory by supplying crafted changesets. Attackers can repeat a table name in a second changeset block with a larger column count, causing sessionUpdateFind() to memset past the undersized aUpdateMask allocation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-119379",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-119379\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libsqlite3-0\nVersion: 3.46.1-7+deb13u2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-119379](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-119379)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-119379**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libsqlite3-0  | 3.46.1-7+deb13u2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-119379](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-119379)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libsqlite3-0@3.46.1-7%2Bdeb13u2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=sqlite3"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-95691-libssl3t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-95691 high vulnerability for libssl3t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: A retransmitted QUIC CRYPTO frame can release packet storage while the TLS record layer retains a direct pointer into that storage causing use after free.  Impact summary: A malicious QUIC server can cause a heap-use-after-free read in the OpenSSL QUIC client. The server can also identify one allocator-adjacent byte through the client's protected Handshake response.  CWE: CWE-416: Use After Free  Description: During CRYPTO stream processing, a pointer into the first frame's memory on the stream is lent to the TLS handshake processing. The memory must remain stable until it is processed and released. However the processing of retransmitted CRYPTO frames could release the memory if the retransmitted frame fully overlapped the existing frame. This then causes use-after-free read when the TLS handshake processing continues.  The use-after-free read can lead to a Denial-of-Service of the client application or a minor leak of information about the heap memory contents that might be overwritten with other data, subsequently allocated by the application, to the peer.  FIPS impact: no The FIPS module is not affected as the QUIC implementation is outside of the OpenSSL FIPS module boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95691",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-95691\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libssl3t64\nVersion: 3.5.7-1~deb13u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-95691](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95691)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-95691**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libssl3t64  | 3.5.7-1~deb13u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-95691](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95691)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssl3t64@3.5.7-1~deb13u3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-95691-openssl-provider-legacy",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-95691 high vulnerability for openssl-provider-legacy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue summary: A retransmitted QUIC CRYPTO frame can release packet storage while the TLS record layer retains a direct pointer into that storage causing use after free.  Impact summary: A malicious QUIC server can cause a heap-use-after-free read in the OpenSSL QUIC client. The server can also identify one allocator-adjacent byte through the client's protected Handshake response.  CWE: CWE-416: Use After Free  Description: During CRYPTO stream processing, a pointer into the first frame's memory on the stream is lent to the TLS handshake processing. The memory must remain stable until it is processed and released. However the processing of retransmitted CRYPTO frames could release the memory if the retransmitted frame fully overlapped the existing frame. This then causes use-after-free read when the TLS handshake processing continues.  The use-after-free read can lead to a Denial-of-Service of the client application or a minor leak of information about the heap memory contents that might be overwritten with other data, subsequently allocated by the application, to the peer.  FIPS impact: no The FIPS module is not affected as the QUIC implementation is outside of the OpenSSL FIPS module boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95691",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-95691\nSeverity: high\nPackage: openssl-provider-legacy\nVersion: 3.5.7-1~deb13u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-95691](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95691)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-95691**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | openssl-provider-legacy  | 3.5.7-1~deb13u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-95691](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-95691)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/openssl-provider-legacy@3.5.7-1~deb13u3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=openssl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-84243-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-84243 high vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The gettext family of functions in the GNU C Library version 2.0 and later accept LANGUAGE environment variable entries that contain '/' or that are equal to \"..\", unless the program is setuid or setgid (AT_SECURE).  An attacker who can set LANGUAGE in the environment of a program that uses gettext can make it load a message catalog (.mo file) from an arbitrary location in the file system.  A crafted .mo file can crash the program through out-of-range offsets, or supply translations whose format directives do not match the arguments passed by the program.  That causes undefined behaviour in the printf family of functions and may allow arbitrary code execution with the privileges of the program.  The safety of message catalogs relies on them being installed in trusted, read-only locations, and the directory traversal bypasses this.  The fix for CVE-2014-0475 rejects \"..\" path components in locale names passed to setlocale or taken from the LC_ALL, LC_* and LANG environment variables.  gettext reads LANGUAGE directly and appends each colon-separated entry to the message catalog directory, so that fix did not cover LANGUAGE.  LANGUAGE is only used when the LC_MESSAGES locale is not \"C\", \"C.\u003cencoding\u003e\" or \"POSIX\", so the attacker must also be able to select another installed locale, for example through LANG or LC_ALL.  Exploitation also requires that the attacker can place the crafted file in a location readable by the target program, and that the environment crosses a trust boundary without the program running as AT_SECURE.  An example is an SSH server that accepts LANGUAGE and LANG from clients through the AcceptEnv directive and restricts an account to a forced command; the attacker may use this to escape the restriction."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-84243",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-84243\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.41-12+deb13u4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-84243](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-84243)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-84243**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libc-bin  | 2.41-12+deb13u4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-84243](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-84243)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libc-bin@2.41-12%2Bdeb13u4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=glibc"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
