                "text": "CVE-2026-78409 high vulnerability for libuuid1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The X-mount.subdir option uses a detached-tree fast path on Linux 6.15 and later and passes the configured subdirectory to open_tree() with AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW. That flag does not stop intermediate symlink traversal or keep resolution inside the newly mounted filesystem. A local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78409",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78409\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libuuid1\nVersion: 2.41.5-0+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-78409](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78409)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78409**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libuuid1  | 2.41.5-0+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-78409](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78409)  |\n"
              },
