            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-127231-libgnutls30t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-127231 medium vulnerability for libgnutls30t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A double free in the X.509 name constraints enforcement of GnuTLS 3.8.13 on all platforms allows a remote attacker to cause a denial of service (application crash) via a certificate chain containing a NameConstraints extension processed while the application is under memory pressure. When an already populated name constraints object is reinitialized, previously freed list pointers are not cleared, so a memory allocation failure precisely at reinitialization leaves a dangling pointer that is freed again during a later cleanup."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-127231",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-127231\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libgnutls30t64\nVersion: 3.8.9-3+deb13u4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-127231](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-127231)",
